# Large example/training data (kept out of git history)
*.npy
examples/medium/SWED/
examples/data/SWED_sample.zip
examples/data/DEM100_Rhine.tif
# Global rasters fetched by docs/examples/11_global_data_on_globe.ipynb. The full-resolution
# originals stay ignored; only the small derived grids below are tracked.
# ersstv5.nc is the exception: it is tracked (19 MB, committed in 5863993) so presets/02 and presets/05
# read it from the checkout instead of fetching it, in CI and on a fresh clone alike. The negation only
# documents that — git already keeps tracking it, which is why it survived this rule in the first place.
examples/data/global/*
!examples/data/global/ersstv5.nc
# Same reasoning for the NCEP temperature climatology and the ETOPO relief: notebooks 11, 12 and 14
# read these from the checkout rather than fetching them, so the docs build executes them offline.
# 0.9 MB for all thirteen, and both sources are US-Government public domain.
!examples/data/global/ncep_tavg_*.tif
!examples/data/global/etopo_relief.tif
docs/examples/examples/

# Claude Code files (kept local only, never tracked)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Planning / design notes (kept local only, never tracked)
planning/
